<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cylon of Athens</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">fl. c. 640–632 BCE</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cylon was an Athenian noble and Olympic victor who tried to make himself tyrant of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a>, probably in 632 BCE, with help from his father-in-law Theagenes, tyrant of Megara. The coup failed; Cylon escaped, but his followers were killed after taking sanctuary, and the curse laid on the Alcmaeonid family, blamed for the killings, troubled Athenian politics for generations.</p></div>
